{
  "title": "NocoBase \u2014 productivity (22,476\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: NocoBase\nDomain: productivity | Scale: large | Stars: 22,476\nProblem: Building business systems (CRM, ERP, internal tools) traditionally requires significant development time and expertise. NocoBase provides an AI-augmented no-code platform that combines WYSIWYG visual building with AI coding agents to accelerate business system creation while maintaining reliability through production-proven infrastructure.\nTarget users: Business operators and non-technical users, Developers and AI coding agents, Enterprise IT teams building internal tools, SMBs needing CRM, ERP, or project management systems, Self-hosted solution adopters\nCore features: WYSIWYG no-code interface for building data models, pages, workflows, and permissions; AI coding agent integration (Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, OpenCode, TRAE); Plugin-based microkernel architecture for extensibility; Built-in workflow automation engine; Fine-grained role-based permissions with field-level access control and audit logs; AI employees integrated into business workflows for task automation; External agent connectivity via MCP, HTTP APIs, and CLI; Multi-source data model support (main DB, external DBs, third-party APIs)\nIntegrations: Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, OpenCode, TRAE, OpenClaw, Hermes, Dify, Coze, n8n, Telegram, WhatsApp, Slack, Gmail, MCP (Model Context Protocol)\nTech stack: React 18, Ant Design 5, Formily + Node.js (>=18), TypeScript + Relational databases (abstracted via ORM, supports external DBs) + Docker, self-hosted, Lerna monorepo, Yarn workspaces\nKey libraries: antd, @formily/antd-v5, react-router-dom, lerna, tsx, dotenv, tsconfig-paths, eslint, @typescript-eslint/parser\nArchitecture: microservices\nDesign lessons:\n- Microkernel plugin architecture allows everything to be a plugin, enabling sustainable system growth without architectural degradation\n- Data-model driven design decouples business data (stored in standard relational structures) from UI, preventing platform lock-in and keeping AI outputs transparent\n- Monorepo with Lerna and Yarn workspaces manages a large multi-package TypeScript codebase across hundreds of plugins and core packages\n- AI and human collaboration is treated as a first-class design concern, with shared permissions and audit infrastructure governing both human and AI agent actions equally",
